B.a3p=new A.c9(B.e2,["What is PadCare and who can use it?","PadCare is a community-led menstrual hygiene platform built to eliminate period poverty and reduce school absenteeism among girls in Uganda. Schoolgirls, parents, guardians, and teachers can use PadCare to access emergency sanitary towels and reusable dignity kits."],t.li)
B.a3t=new A.c9(B.e2,["Is my pad request completely confidential?","Yes, absolutely. PadCare protects the privacy of every girl. Requests never require a student's personal name, class, or age. A unique confidential reference code and secret 4-digit pickup PIN are generated on your device for private collection."],t.li)
B.a3v=new A.c9(B.e2,["How do school pickups work with Senior Woman Teachers?","Senior Woman Teachers are verified female mentors stationed at participating schools (such as Ediofe Girls School, Oli Primary School, and St. Mary's Secondary). When a request is approved, the student or guardian presents their confidential 4-digit PIN to collect the package discreetly."],t.li)
B.a3q=new A.c9(B.e2,["Does PadCare work without an active internet connection?","Yes! PadCare is engineered offline-first. You can browse pickup points, check educational hygiene articles, and submit local requests completely offline. Any actions you submit are queued safely on your device and synchronized once an internet connection is detected."],t.li)
B.a3o=new A.c9(B.e2,["How do Mobile Money (MoMo) donations support schoolgirls?","Through MTN MoMo and Airtel Money, community members can sponsor hygiene supplies directly. A 3,000 UGX contribution provides an emergency pack of disposable pads, while 15,000 UGX funds a complete reusable kit lasting up to 12 months."],t.li)
B.a3u=new A.c9(B.e2,["What is included in a reusable PadCare dignity kit?","Each reusable kit contains 4 to 6 washable, antimicrobial cloth pads, leak-proof storage pouches, antibacterial laundry soap, and an illustrated menstrual hygiene booklet."],t.li)
B.a3r=new A.c9(B.e2,["How can our school or health clinic register as a pad provider?",'Schools, health centers, and community organizations can submit an application via the "Register as a Pad Provider" button in their Profile tab. Once reviewed and verified, staff gain access to manage inventory and review local requests.'],t.li)
B.a3s=new A.c9(B.e2,["Who created PadCare?","PadCare was developed in Uganda by Dan Mungufeni (GTNationDEV) and Abeti Acadri Nicholas to solve real menstrual hygiene barriers in Arua City and rural schools across the region."],t.li)
